WEBVTT

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.320
Okay.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.190
This is the final screw.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.730
I'll entrust it to you, Serufu.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.600
Are you sure?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.730
Of course.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.810
Back then...

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.980
when, just by chance...

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.140
I asked you to put in that screw, Serufu...

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.290
I think that action has brought us to today.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.880
That's why.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.000
Yes, ma'am!

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.360
It's done!

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.940
You did that really well!

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.600
Thank you!

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.610
Purin!

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.830
Thank you for helping.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.270
Sure.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.530
This is our...

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.550
secret hideout!

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.360
And then last night...

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.210
Oh!

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.900
Did they finish the tree house?

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.660
It's pretty legit, don't you think?

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.420
That's really amazing!

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:50.020
Congratulations on the 
completion of the tree house.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.250
Everyone... Good job!

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.910
Good job!

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:04.750
The smell of wood is wonderful, isn't it?

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.280
It is.

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.780
But these floorboards...

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.260
Oh! I made that part!

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.720
I thought so.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.440
The screws are all lopsided, and 
there's a big gap between the boards.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:18.450
Crooked

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:18.450
Crooked

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:18.450
Gap

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.130
Why are you acting bashful?

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:25.370
But this gives it character, 
which is good, right, club leader?

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:27.760
That's right.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.370
Hikage-san, the stained glass you made...

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.930
is so beautiful!

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.150
Th-Thank you.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.940
Suride-san, the lampshade you 
made is incredibly lovely, too.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:42.130
Thanks.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.440
You can call me Purin if you want.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.190
P-Purin-san.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.530
Please call me Takumin.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:51.710
Takumin-san!

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.910
The shelves Jobko made
 match this room really well!

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.280
Of course!

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.930
Club leader, I compliment the wall slats 
and roof shingles you laid.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:08.470
As usual, spoken as though 
she's the superior one.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.760
And Shii, the ceiling frame you built is perfect!

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.910
Receiving such words of 
praise is an honor, meow!

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:21.240
Let's have a sleepover party 
together in the secret hideout!

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.390
Sounds good!

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.450
It's too small for that, isn't it?

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.580
Then just me and Purin!

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.560
Wh-Why would it end up like that?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.480
<b>Step 12
"DIY" Means Friendship, Always and Forever!</b>

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:35.130
Summer vacation begins tomorrow.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:40.540
Students, please endeavor to 
lead a well-regulated life.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:47.920
Tackle studying, club activities, and 
recreation with everything you've got.

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.700
And then, in the new term...

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.900
Is it almost time?

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.540
Yes. They said that the YuuVoc end-of-term
 assembly should finish around noon.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.470
Shii's here.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.230
Kouki Kokoro...

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.420
has arrived!

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.470
Oh! A kunoichi!

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:16.780
Shii-chan! Welcome!

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:19.470
Thank you for inviting me, meow.

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.020
Hold on! Kouki-san!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.240
I told you to enter properly through 
the Gata Girls' school gate, didn't I?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.190
I ditched security, so it'll be fine!

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.080
That's <i>not</i> the issue here!

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:33.580
Purin! Welcome!

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.660
We're all ready here!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.280
Thank you for being kind enough 
to extend an invitation to me.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:48.180
Now that everyone is here, 
are we ready for a toast?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.040
Yes!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.260
Yes, meow!

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:53.670
It's a splendid tree house!

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:57.180
Your secret hideout is complete.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.060
You all worked so hard 
without ever giving up.

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:03.110
You're all splendid as well!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.980
Now, we begin a celebration of the 
completion of the secret hideout...

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.740
and also a farewell party for Jobko-san...

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.370
Cheers!

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.370
Cheers!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.320
We've prepared senbetsu for Jobko-san.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.810
Senbetsu?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.980
I guess you could call it a "farewell gift."

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.650
Oh, I see!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.900
It's sukonbu.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.210
Please eat as much as you like!

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.130
Wow!

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:53.060
<b>Sukonbu         Sukonbu         Sukonbu         Sukonbu</b>

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.230
Many sukonbu!

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:54.990
Thank you, Haruko!

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.570
This is from me!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:58.270
What?

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.920
Jobko-chan

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.920
Thank you

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.390
Is this me?

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.130
It's incredible, Serufu-san!

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.560
You should draw me cuter.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.110
Purin made the frame!

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.810
Isn't it pretty?

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:17.070
Since you went to all the trouble, 
I suppose I'll accept it.

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:21.280
I wasn't sure what would be best, but...

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.300
It's a complete set of the 
<i>Sunflower Girls</i> manga.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.930
Did we get the same thing?

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.130
Oh, no.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:33.890
I got her a full set of the source 
work, the <i>SunGirls</i> novels.

00:06:34.690 --> 00:06:36.300
That's a relief.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:38.860
Try reading both.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:41.970
I think it'll help you with
 reading and writing Japanese.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:43.950
Thank you so much!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:47.020
Takumin! Club leader!

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.410
This is what you could call "proselytizing."

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.390
When did you learn a word like that?

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:57.110
Mine is a gift from my home country.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.440
Roar!

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.530
Th-Thank you, Shii.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.520
Even after you get home to America,

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.960
don't forget us, okay?

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.160
Even if I tried to forget...

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:12.520
I'd never be able to forget you!

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.260
Serufu! Are you okay?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.610
Jobko-san.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.470
Please use this handkerchief.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.780
It's not like I'm crying, 
but I'll borrow it anyway.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.090
Ow...

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.760
If all of you get lonely...

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.910
I wouldn't mind coming back right away.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.750
Yes, please come whenever you'd like.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.450
Seriously. You just can't 
be honest, can you?

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.530
Well, if you want me to, 
I don't mind coming back!

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.270
Jobkocchi, you're so cute, meow.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:00.540
Club

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:06.040
To think that a plan to increase membership 
would turn into a tree house...

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.790
Yeah, for real!

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:12.290
But, in the end, we didn't 
get any new members.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:16.330
Yeah. We won't be able to 
receive club funds anymore.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.940
But I say, "I guess that's okay!"

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.550
After all, it only means that we 
won't get club funds anymore.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:27.020
That will put us in quite a bind, though.

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:31.070
Still, it's just as you say, Serufu-san.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.270
Yeah.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:36.060
We can just keep making small 
things and selling them.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.720
And if we gather things 
that others don't need...

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.690
...everything will work out somehow, meow!

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:45.200
The same way that we built 
this secret hideout... right?

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:46.920
Exactly.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.370
I...

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:56.090
am really glad I joined the DIY club!

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.830
S-So am I!

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:58.780
Me, too!

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.120
Me, too!

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.140
Meeting all of you has 
made me really happy, too.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.350
I'll be counting on you from now on, too!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.700
Of course!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.700
Meow!

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:13.480
Excuse me...

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:18.640
We were wondering what the DIY club is like.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.900
Can we go in the tree house?

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.160
Please do!

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.790
Thank you!

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.510
Okay. Does that about do it?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.420
Jobko-san, this is the last suitcase.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.560
Shall I close it up?

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.600
Okay.

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:44.760
Stop right there!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.880
Mama?

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.240
You forgot something.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.110
<b>Sukonbu         Sukonbu         Sukonbu          Sukonbu</b>

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.100
You like these, right?

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.700
Take them with you.

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:56.420
Wow!

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.390
So many, many sukonbu!

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.830
Your sukonbu have doubled, haven't they?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.870
Thank you, Pudding's mom!

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.600
You are welcome.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:10.370
Miku, I'm headed off on a 
business trip to Norway.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.930
You'll be here on your own for about a week.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.640
I'll be looking forward 
to souvenirs from Norway.

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.380
Oil-packed sardines, right?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.890
About this hammock...

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:20.690
I know.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:23.640
"A bird, departing, leaves 
its nest unsullied," right?

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:28.260
I'll arrange for some contractors to come later,
 so there's nothing to worry about!

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.710
There's no need.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.270
I'll leave it just as it is,

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.900
so come back whenever you like.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.630
I will!

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.170
Bye, then, Jobko-chan.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.770
Good job!

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:54.500
Thank you for everything!

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.260
The ohagi was delicious!

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.640
I'll make it again!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.350
How lovely! How lovely! How lovely!

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.010
It's perfect, Pudding's mom!

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.630
Hey, Jobko-chan?

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:08.760
What is it?

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.140
Are you sure I shouldn't come 
to the airport to see you off?

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:14.520
It's fine.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.700
I've hired a limousine, 
so I won't get lost or anything.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:19.700
Still...

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.290
Plus, if you do something like that...

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.860
it'll make it harder for me to leave, right?

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.330
That's true.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.950
I think... I'm going to be sort of lonely.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.310
That's a rare bit of honesty.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.050
It's okay to have some 
days like that, right?

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.690
The completed secret hideout...

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:46.050
doesn't look anything like the 
one I built with my mama...

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.790
but the fun I had while 
making it was the same!

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:54.020
No, it was even more fun!

00:11:55.950 --> 00:12:01.060
The reason I came to Japan to study was 
so I could get away from Papa.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:07.940
Since Mama passed away,
 Papa is depressed more often...

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:12.700
and he talks to me less...

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:21.760
When I get back home, I think I'll tell 
him about how I built a tree house!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:24.440
I'm sure that will make him happy.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.020
Yeah!

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.230
Saying what we really mean...

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:34.900
would make things easier 
for both you and me, Pudding.

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:36.520
That's true.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:40.810
Like, you know how Serufu can be sort 
of inconsiderate sometimes, right?

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:41.730
I know.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.030
She's always been clumsy,

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:45.440
and she gets hurt a lot.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.160
I just can't leave her on her own.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:53.700
But since she's like that, I guess 
you'd call it looking after her...

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:56.330
Being with her makes me happy.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.160
Then why are you always all 
"puri puri" with anger?

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.070
Why?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:07.450
It's because Serufu can be so 
inconsiderate that I'm like this!

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.400
I know.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:11.670
Oh, no! I've been a little too honest!

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:14.930
Then I shall also say something honest.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:19.130
I would like you to install the new OS.

00:13:21.790 --> 00:13:25.220
You really can't read the air, can you?

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.090
Jobko-chan, see you again sometime!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.570
She left, huh?

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.340
Yes, she left.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.320
And now, we're going, too!

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:23.580
Going where?

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:31.550
Miku-san, it is hot outside.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:35.760
Please be sure to hydrate 
and be careful on your way.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:40.360
After your OS update, even your 
voice changed, didn't it?

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.610
Life is like a flowing river.

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:43.440
I'm going now.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.140
All living things are—

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.200
Why are we at the DIY club?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.480
We've got the day off today, don't we?

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:53.460
We're missing something.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.780
Missing something?

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:56.110
This.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.290
<b>Club</b>

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.750
Oh! A swing!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.390
You designed this, Purin?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.600
That's right. We'll make it together.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:07.560
Oh! But the materials...

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:13.130
I feel bad for the first 
generation of members...

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.630
but it should be okay to pull 
off a few more boards, right?

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.860
That's true.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:20.090
Oh! And...

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.770
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:24.470
There's this, too!

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:26.710
Purin! That's...

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:27.890
I kept it aside.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.480
Come on. Don't just stand there dazed.
 Pull up some boards!

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.640
O-Okay!

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.660
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.670
Be careful doing it, okay?

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:36.000
Will do!

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:44.650
And I told you to be careful, too.

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.200
What is it?

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:54.180
I was thinking that it's been a while since 
I last put a bandage on you, Serufu.

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:58.600
Oh, that's true. It used 
to be every day, right?

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.750
It wasn't <i>just</i> every day, 
it was <i>several</i> times a day!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:05.690
But for me that was...

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.120
Purin?

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.000
I-It's nothing!

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.480
Okay. We're doing this!

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.330
Yeah!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.820
Back

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:15.820
Seat

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:33.160
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:37.920
Water-based

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:37.920
Stain

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:04.600
It's done!

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.690
Purin, sit down!

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.780
Serufu, you should sit on it first.

00:17:08.780 --> 00:17:10.670
Go ahead! Go ahead!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:12.640
Th-Then, let's sit together!

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.150
Oh! That would work!

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.600
<b>Serufu • Miku</b>

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:30.340
Somehow, you seem super happy, Purin.

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:33.560
You know, Serufu...

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:40.570
There's something... I have to tell you.

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:41.980
What is it?

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:48.560
I said that DIY was all moldy, 
useless stuff, but...

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:52.580
I've had so much fun!

00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:56.670
Thank you for inviting me, Serufu.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.500
Purin...

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.630
And...

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.230
I'm sorry.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:03.910
What?

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.310
What did you say?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.230
Stupid Serufu.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:11.510
Oh, Purin. You get angry so quickly.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.770
And whose fault is that?

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.630
Wha?!

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:17.440
And anyway, you're the 
one who said it, Serufu!

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.580
Hey, Purin...

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:27.580
<b>Congratulations
On entering</b>

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:23.820
now that I'm a middle schooler,

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.260
I'm going to get the point that
 I can do everything on my own!

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:27.150
What?

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:30.800
So, I'll be okay now!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:41.040
It's not like I hate looking 
after you, Serufu.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.480
Even if you wanted to keep 
depending on me for...

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.550
Did I say that?

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.190
You <i>did</i> say that!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:50.230
W-Well, it's okay, right? 
Since it's in the past.

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:54.120
Honestly, you...

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:57.570
Then you don't remember this either, do you?

00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:00.560
Oh! A secret hideout!

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:02.400
A secret hideout?

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.360
I'd like to build one. Up in a tree!

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:10.540
And I'd hang your wind chime there, Purin!

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:14.180
What? Did I say that?

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.520
I knew it.

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:19.890
And I'll bet you've lost the
 wind chime I gave you, too.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:21.410
I have that!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:22.270
What?!

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:24.650
Because it's something you gave me, Purin!

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.130
I kept it stored away really carefully.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.010
It's a treasure of mine!

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.660
I know!

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.850
I could go get it and we could hang it now!

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:44.920
Wha? But since you still have it,
 y-you should just leave it as it is!

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.640
Really? But the secret hideout could...

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:49.170
You treasure it, right?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.660
Then keep it where it is.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.540
O-Okay.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.050
Club

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.850
If we want a wind chime for the secret hideout,

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.970
then we can just make one.

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:03.930
I thought we could use these.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.980
Oh, did you pick all that up at the beach?

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:07.880
That's right.

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:10.200
Wow!

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.530
They're so pretty!

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.640
They seem like they'd make a nice sound.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.390
Okay!

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:20.270
We're making a new wind chime!

00:20:21.060 --> 00:20:21.740
Purin!

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.300
Do it...

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:37.120
yourself!
